{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Omega_{X/S} = 0$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Omega_{X/S} = 0$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-unramified-omega-zero}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:aae5fc882a52cd8f0ce957ace8ff31d2909c99a585ebcaa9bac2d2af75e222ef", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:14befd652626bfc4bb8187d946d39aa3d2afe05ba143c5430eb33726ccdb1b66", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is unramified if and only if <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type\nand <MATH_0004>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is G-unramified if and only if <MATH_0006> is locally of finite presentation\nand <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a3a4115b9cf94d87d8320e104725fae96885e387a4764dd0b55ccef58fba3ef2", "unit_id": "tag:02G5:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Omega_{A/R} = 0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-differentials-affine}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b73979630cea9227c791b666336d0a8a635cae4c65b831f9e1968f32f3bfaae", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ff209586040726a37e9be558cc3e0b93161c57e937d8cb8f9e856460a9912c20", "source_text": "By definition a ring map <MATH_0001> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0001>G-unramified)\nif and only if it is of finite type (resp.<SPACE_0002>finite presentation)\nand <MATH_0002>. Hence the lemma follows\ndirectly from the definitions and Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:98126399b40fe308d3e8d0e12eea19387a98bbb02ec59689bb9b251b9194c5f3", "unit_id": "tag:02G5:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8b8b966b1c32d42b17995ae13d4b5f18c566e92f16b9acaff66657980930ab03", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that there is no separation or quasi-compactness hypotheses in the\ndefinition. Hence the question of being unramified is local in nature on\nthe source. Here is the precise result.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872160525d778db97b0665c1ee1e1ba566223cdaf36bb784688ef2a59cafeb30", "unit_id": "tag:02G3:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0005": "$f(U) \\subset V$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0007": "$S = \\bigcup_{j \\in J} V_j$", "MATH_0008": "$f^{-1}(V_j) = \\bigcup_{i \\in I_j} U_i$", "MATH_0009": "$U_i \\to V_j$", "MATH_0010": "$j\\in J, i\\in I_j$", "MATH_0011": "$S = \\bigcup_{j \\in J} V_j$", "MATH_0012": "$f^{-1}(V_j) = \\bigcup_{i \\in I_j} U_i$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(V_j) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0014": "$j\\in J, i\\in I_j$", "MATH_0015": "$f$", "MATH_0016": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0017": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0018": "$f(U) \\subset V$", "MATH_0019": "$f|_U : U \\to V$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ ", "SPACE_0004": "\\ ", "SPACE_0005": "\\ ", "SPACE_0006": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-unramified-characterize}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:831157cffc4f322e7a359b1d2895997bfe94b41d1a431cf27d30599a8144b2c2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c60104d4cf872b504f2bb235cf7d19eb0ddb5023fb254ee5b40881ffb2c91125", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The morphism <MATH_0002> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0001>G-unramified).\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004>\nwith <MATH_0005> the ring map\n<MATH_0006> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0002>G-unramified).\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nand open coverings <MATH_0008> such\nthat each of the morphisms <MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010>\nis unramified (resp.<SPACE_0003>G-unramified).\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0011>\nand affine open coverings <MATH_0012> such\nthat the ring map <MATH_0013> is\nunramified (resp.<SPACE_0004>G-unramified), for all <MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0015> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0005>G-unramified) then for\nany open subschemes <MATH_0016>, <MATH_0017> with <MATH_0018>\nthe restriction <MATH_0019> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0006>G-unramified).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:78e8721559553afff0cab672914a4026fcc59369d7562790bb0ca81c35e41a74", "unit_id": "tag:02G6:statement"}
